cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, cite it as described below. The accompanying manuscript is not published yet, so no article DOI is asserted."
title: "Galaxy-HRGuard: three-state reliability measurement for wrist heart rate"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-08
type: software
license: LicenseRef-Proprietary-Pending
license-url: "https://github.com/phr-devil/Galaxy-HRGuard/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/phr-devil/Galaxy-HRGuard"
url: "https://github.com/phr-devil/Galaxy-HRGuard"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a three-state reliability measurement for wrist
  heart rate. Windows in which the device reports a value are labelled correct
  or wrong against a chest-belt reference at a 10 bpm threshold; windows in
  which the device declines to report are kept in the population as a third
  state. The wrong-output share among unreliable windows, its participant-
  clustered bootstrap interval, the availability and conditional-accuracy
  decomposition of full correct coverage, and the exploratory analyses of
  Table 3 of the accompanying manuscript are all computed here.
keywords:
  - wearable sensors
  - photoplethysmography
  - heart rate
  - reliability measurement
  - missing data
  - selective prediction
  - reproducibility
authors:
